                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1]Basic Info[/h1] \n[b]Genre: Platformer[/b] \n[b]Difficulty: Medium-Hard[/b] \n\n[h1]Gameplay[/h1]\n[b]Rating:[/b]8/10\n\n[b]Contrary to what the store page says, a controller is NOT required to play this game, as it is playable with just the keyboard.[/b]\n[i]You may want to use a controller though, as it will most likely allow for more precise and accurate movement.[/i]\n\n\nYou play as a trainee ninja from the Mad Dojo and your task is to get from your dojo to the finish line to prove to your sensei you have what it takes to become a real ninja. \nWhile this task may seem simple, your journey is filled with obstacles, such as spikes, bamboo sticks and acid. Luckily you have your throwing stars which can cut down bamboo and your agility which allows you to double jump and hang onto walls. Unfortunately, since you are in training, everything kills you with one touch.\nAnd your sensei is impatient, so you have to complete the levels as fast as possible, not only to challenge yourself, but also all of the other potential ninja trainees (on the leader boards), trying to become real ninjas.  \n\nThe levels get progressively harder by introducing new obstacles, more obstacles and harder placement of the obstacles. There is a total of 30 levels in the game, even though I have yet to pass level 10.\n\n[h1]Narrative[/h1]\n[b]Rating:[/b]0/10\nThe game has no narrative other than what is found on the store page.\nI would have personally liked if there were some narrative to explain the reason why we are training to be a ninja and try to get past these obstacles.\n\n[h1]Visual Presentation[/h1]\n[b]Rating:[/b]8/10\nThe game uses an 16-bit pixel cartoon art-style. It runs on the Unity game engine and will run smoothly on most machines. \n\n[h1]Audio Presentation[/h1]\n[b]Rating:[/b]8/10\nThe soundtrack for this game is varied and has an eastern-inspired theme, which fits very well with the ninja theme.\nThe sound effects are top quality and fits the genre, style and theme very well.\n\n[h1]Final Score[/h1]\n[b]Rating:[/b]6/10\nThis game is challenging, difficult even. It will challenge you to try just one more time. Just one more death before you exit. At times you will be frustrated, mostly because you know you have the skills to finish the level but just keep getting the timing wrong. It is a great game to boot up and play for 5 to 10 minutes, but you can also easily spend hours trying to complete some levels.\n\n[code]Submitted for [url=http://steamcommunity.com/groups/elitegives]Elite Giveaways[/url] and [url=http://steamcommunity.com/groups/semeigaming]Semeicardia Gaming[/url].[/code]",
